<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Mono Grid</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #101214;
      --panel: #171a1d;
      --panel-strong: #1e2328;
      --text: #edf0f2;
      --muted: #a0adb6;
      --line: #283039;
      --accent: #95f479;
      --shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      background:
        linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.05) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.05) 1px, transparent 1px),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #0f1215 0%, #121518 100%);
      background-size: 22px 22px, 22px 22px, auto;
      font-family: Consolas, "Lucida Console", monospace;
    }
    a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .shell { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    .topbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 10;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      background: rgba(16, 18, 20, 0.88);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(40, 48, 57, 0.95);
    }
    .topbar-inner,
    .footer {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 18px 0;
    }
    .brand {
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .brand span { color: var(--accent); }
    .nav, .footer-nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 18px;
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(280px, 0.8fr);
      gap: 22px;
      padding: 58px 0 20px;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .tag {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--accent);
      background: rgba(149, 244, 121, 0.06);
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 18px 0 14px;
      font-size: clamp(38px, 7vw, 84px);
      line-height: 0.92;
    }
    .lead {
      max-width: 620px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      margin: 0 0 24px;
    }
    .buttons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 0 16px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--panel);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .button.primary {
      background: var(--accent);
      border-color: var(--accent);
      color: #091105;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .panel, .card, .feed {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: rgba(23, 26, 29, 0.92);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .panel { border-radius: 18px; padding: 20px; }
    .status-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }
    .status {
      padding: 12px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--panel-strong);
    }
    .status strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      font-size: 18px;
    }
    section { padding: 20px 0; }
    .section-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: end;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
    .section-head h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 36px);
    }
    .section-head p,
    .card p,
    .feed p,
    .footer-copy {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .card {
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 18px;
    }
    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: 18px;
      color: var(--accent);
    }
    .feed {
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 18px;
    }
    .log {
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }
    .log-item {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr;
      gap: 14px;
      padding-top: 12px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .log-item:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }
    .stamp { color: var(--accent); }
    .footer-wrap {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      margin-top: 20px;
      padding-bottom: 38px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .hero, .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .topbar-inner, .section-head, .footer { display: block; }
      .nav, .footer-nav { margin-top: 14px; }
      .log-item { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="shell topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">Mono <span>Grid</span></a>
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#services">Services</a>
        <a href="#stack">Stack</a>
        <a href="#logbook">Logbook</a>
        <a href="#footer">Index</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="top" class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="tag">Operational layouts and route indexing</span>
        <h1>Private-facing service surfaces, documented like systems.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Mono Grid publishes compact tooling notes, hosting references, and support
          materials for small environments that value repeatability over presentation noise.
        </p>
        <div class="buttons">
          <a class="button primary" href="#services">Browse services</a>
          <a class="button" href="#logbook">Read logbook</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel">
        <strong>Current service window</strong>
        <p>Support queue and route review updates are published in short rotating batches for existing operators.</p>
        <div class="status-grid">
          <div class="status"><strong>03</strong>active indexes</div>
          <div class="status"><strong>11</strong>guide revisions</div>
          <div class="status"><strong>2 hr</strong>ticket review block</div>
          <div class="status"><strong>99.9%</strong>mirrored availability</div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="services">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Service index</h2>
        <p>Operational material is grouped by surface type rather than by product line, which keeps updates short and predictable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Edge routing</h3>
          <p>Reference notes for ingress shaping, maintenance windows, and operator-facing fallback logic.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Access publishing</h3>
          <p>Static pages and gated paths for teams that need stable distribution without a large content footprint.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Review lanes</h3>
          <p>Short-cycle verification of service changes, configuration drift, and low-noise operational adjustments.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="stack">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Reference stack</h2>
        <p>The public-facing site stays intentionally spare while still offering enough shape to look like a maintained technical property.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feed">
        <p>
          Documentation surfaces, mirror nodes, rollout notes, and intake forms are kept on
          separate cycles. Public pages surface only high-level status and category-level guidance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="logbook">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Logbook</h2>
        <p>Minimal release-style notes that read like a maintained operations page instead of a placeholder splash screen.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feed">
        <div class="log">
          <div class="log-item">
            <div class="stamp">2026.04</div>
            <div>Reorganized support materials by intake mode and reduced duplicate operator notes.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="log-item">
            <div class="stamp">2026.03</div>
            <div>Consolidated edge review checklists and refreshed public system index copy.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="log-item">
            <div class="stamp">2026.02</div>
            <div>Moved archive-ready materials into a lighter publication cycle for smaller deployments.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <div id="footer" class="footer-wrap">
    <footer class="shell footer">
      <div>
        <strong>Mono Grid</strong>
        <p class="footer-copy">A compact technical index for route-aware service materials and lightweight operator notes.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#top">Top</a>
        <a href="#services">Services</a>
        <a href="#stack">Stack</a>
        <a href="#logbook">Logbook</a>
      </nav>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
